From e237d03be0bdf491ca53cbac2cbb094355e0429a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:24:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] aimesh: centre the node model name over its MAC line

Owner item ("Image Alignment"). Stock right-aligns both lines of the node card's
info block - .model_info_bg is text-align:right and .model_name is a flex row
with justify-content:flex-end, inside a shrink-to-fit absolute box pinned
upper-right - so the two lines share only their RIGHT edge. "RT-BE96U" at 24px
is narrower than "MAC | 10:7C:61:85:FE:F0" at 12px, so the name hangs off to the
right of the MAC it is supposed to sit over.

Centred on both axes in reaper_content.css section 11 (stock page and stock
aimesh CSS untouched, per the override rule): whichever line is wider sets the
box width and the other centres against it, so it also holds when the widths
invert on a long model name. The box stays pinned upper-right - nothing moves
but the alignment inside it.

Measured headless (Chrome, the shipped stock rules plus the shipped override):
RT-BE96U name centre 347 vs MAC centre 334 before = 12 px right of centre, 334
vs 334 after. GT-BE98_PRO measures 0 both ways - at these font sizes that name
is exactly as wide as the MAC line, so the rule is a no-op there rather than a
regression. .model_info_bg appears only in aimesh_topology.html, so the override
cannot reach another page.

NOT BUILT. AiMesh is metal-only-validatable (the mock cannot render the topology
page), so the owner confirms on device.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
index 3f9a6a16ea..9f918f7802 100644
--- a/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
+++ b/release/src/router/www/reaper/reaper_content.css
@@ -377,6 +377,16 @@ div[id$="_Block_PC"],div[id$="_Block_PC"] div,div[id$="_Block_PC"] a{
 .primary_info_bg > .icon_bg .translucent_bg{background:none!important;height:100%!important}
 .primary_info_bg > .item_space{background:transparent!important;position:relative;z-index:1}
 .primary_info_bg > .item_bg.location{background:transparent!important;position:relative;z-index:1}
+/* 2026-08-11: centre the model name over the MAC line. Stock right-aligns both
+   (.model_info_bg text-align:right, .model_name justify-content:flex-end) inside
+   a shrink-to-fit absolute box, so the two lines only line up on their right
+   edge - "RT-BE96U" (24px) is narrower than "MAC | 10:7C:..." (12px) and hangs
+   off to the right of it. Centring BOTH axes means whichever line is wider sets
+   the box and the other centres against it, so it also holds for a long model
+   name (GT-BE98_PRO) where the widths invert. The box stays pinned upper-right;
+   nothing moves but the alignment inside it. */
+.model_info_bg{text-align:center!important}
+.model_info_bg > .model_name{justify-content:center!important}
 
